Rule 1 (tuple of types to check against should not contain duplicate elements)
{v_2 : tuple(dtype ⊎ str)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : ∀j ∈ [i + 1, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≠ v_2[j]
>>
Rule 2 (kind string should not be an invalid keyword from tensor or reduction operations)
{v_2 : str} |= v_2 ≠ "ii" ∧ v_2 ≠ "ii->i" ∧ v_2 ≠ "i,j->ij" ∧ v_2 ≠ "bij,bjk->bik" ∧ v_2 ≠ "...ij->...ji" ∧ v_2 ≠ "none" ∧ v_2 ≠ "sum" ∧ v_2 ≠ "max" ∧ v_2 ≠ "min" ∧ v_2 ≠ "mean" ∧ v_2 ≠ "relu" ∧ v_2 ≠ "tanh" ∧ v_2 ≠ "sigmoid" ∧ v_2 ≠ "softmax" ∧ v_2 ≠ "gelu" ∧ v_2 ≠ "NHWC" ∧ v_2 ≠ "NCHW" ∧ v_2 ≠ "HWIO" ∧ v_2 ≠ "OIHW" ∧ v_2 ≠ "valid" ∧ v_2 ≠ "same"
>>
Rule 3 (tuple of kind strings should not contain invalid keywords)
{v_2 : tuple(str)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≠ "ii" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "ii->i" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "i,j->ij" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "bij,bjk->bik" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "...ij->...ji" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "none" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "sum" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "max" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "min" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "mean" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "relu" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "tanh" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "sigmoid" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "softmax" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "gelu" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "NHWC" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "NCHW" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "HWIO" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "OIHW" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "valid" ∧ v_2[i] ≠ "same"
>>
Rule 4 (Input dtype parameter should represent a valid numpy/jax data type index)
{v_1 : dtype} |= v_1 ≥ 0 ∧ v_1 ≤ 10
>>
Rule 5 (If checking against a single target dtype, both must be valid data type indices)
{v_1 : dtype, v_2 : dtype} |= v_1 ≥ 0 ∧ v_1 ≤ 10 ∧ v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 ≤ 10
>>
Rule 6 (If checking against a list of target dtypes, the target tuple must be non-empty and all elements must be valid data type indices)
{v_1 : dtype, v_2 : tuple(dtype)} |= v_1 ≥ 0 ∧ v_1 ≤ 10 ∧ v_2.len ≥ 1 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_2[i] ≤ 10
